Forgejo API fixtures (tests/forge.test.sh, tests/solo.test.sh, tests/run-cmd.test.sh).

ALL OF THESE ARE SPEC-DERIVED, not recorded: no API token for forgejo.internal
existed while they were written, and the API refuses anonymous calls ("Only
signed in user is allowed to call APIs."). Each is shaped from the server's own
OpenAPI document - Forgejo 17.0.1 (gitea-1.22.0), http://forgejo.internal/swagger.v1.json -
using exactly its definitions and field names:

  user.json                         User                 GET /user
  pull.json, pulls-page1.json,
  pulls-page2.json                  PullRequest          GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/pulls[/{index}]
  status.json                       CombinedStatus       GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/commits/{ref}/status
  protection-*.json                 BranchProtection     GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/branch_protections/{name}
  protections-*.json                []BranchProtection   GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/branch_protections
  reviews.json                      []PullReview         GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/pulls/{index}/reviews
  not-found.json                    APINotFound (404)    the not-found answer
  forbidden.json, merge-conflict.json  APIError          403 / 409 answers

Values (shas, ids, names, timestamps) are invented; emails are empty. Replace
any of these with a recorded answer (token in ~/.config/cel/forge/
